MobileGlues: the encoded ASTC blocks uploaded from memory where uploads from a buffer land wrong.

A Pixel 10's PowerVR drew the sprites the encoder made with their blocks scrambled (Pocket Foundry #65): its
compressed uploads from a pixel unpack buffer land in the wrong places, in every level size tried from 2048x2048 to
16384x256, where the same blocks uploaded from memory land right. Where the encoder is first built, blocks that each
say where they belong are uploaded from a buffer into a level as wide as the game's atlases and drawn back; where one
lands wrong, that's logged, and each batch's encoded blocks are read back and uploaded from memory.

